gsipper (1.3.33-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop showing the 'gsipper is ready' notification when the
    user clicks the panel icon / app-grid icon after the window
    was hidden to tray. Two-sided fix:
      - Extension: drop the custom Show() D-Bus method call,
        route the panel click through the standard
        org.freedesktop.Application.Activate D-Bus interface
        (auto-exposed by GApplication). gnome-shell injects an
        xdg-activation token into the call's platform_data,
        which GApplication then passes to GTK as part of the
        activate signal — so present() raises the window
        without the compositor treating it as focus-stealing.
        Falls back to the custom Show() if Activate errors out.
      - App: extract activation-token / desktop-startup-id
        from the command-line signal's platform_data and feed
        it into Gdk.Display.set_startup_notification_id +
        XDG_ACTIVATION_TOKEN environment, so app-grid launches
        (which always go through HANDLES_COMMAND_LINE) get the
        same treatment.
    do_activate is also smarter about re-activations now:
    only honour 'Start minimized' the first time the window
    is built; subsequent activations always present the
    window (the user is explicitly asking it to come back).
    extension/metadata.json bumped 7 -> 8.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 20 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.3.32-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * _build_dial_uri now strips formatting characters (spaces,
    dashes, parens, dots) from phone-number dial targets before
    pasting them into the user-part of the SIP URI. Dialling a
    contact stored as '+49 5254 9306791' used to produce
    'sip:0049 5254 9306791@callagent.pro' — pjsua2's
    Call_makeCall raises pjsua2.Error on unescaped whitespace in
    the URI. Now: keep digits + '+' / '*' / '#', then apply the
    '+' -> '00' E.164 transform as before, so the same contact
    dials as 'sip:004952549306791@callagent.pro'. sip: / sips: /
    tel: URIs pass through untouched (user knows what they're
    doing).

