gsipper (1.3.27-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Mic-mute toggle in the in-call pane. A small circular toggle
    appears below the duration label when the call is connected
    (and is hidden during incoming/ringing/calling/ended). The
    icon flips between microphone-sensitivity-high-symbolic and
    microphone-disabled-symbolic as you toggle. Under the hood
    the toggle calls SipEndpoint.set_mic_muted() -> SipCall
    .set_mic_muted(), which connect/disconnect the local capture
    media from the remote call audio in pjsua2's conference
    bridge. Mute state is preserved across mid-call media
    re-bridges (hold/resume, codec renegotiation): if you muted
    before the second onCallMediaState fires, we re-tear the
    mic→peer link as soon as the new audio path comes up.
  * Recording shows up in Recent without a manual refresh. The
    Recent row was being rendered the instant the call ended
    (via 'state==ended' -> calls.refresh()), but the MP3 file
    didn't exist yet at that point — ffmpeg was still running
    in a daemon thread. Added a 'recording-ready' handler that
    fires on GLib.idle_add once the MP3 lands on disk, and
    MainWindow re-refreshes Recent in response.
  * ffmpeg conversion errors now log the actual stderr instead
    of swallowing them. If your distro ships an ffmpeg without
    libmp3lame, you'll now see 'Unknown encoder libmp3lame' (or
    similar) in the gsipper log and can install
    libavcodec-extra to fix it.

