gsipper (1.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SIP User-Agent header reformatted from 'gsipper <version>' to
    'gsipper/<version>'. Many SIP-server admin UIs derive the
    'Device' column from the first space-delimited token, which
    silently dropped the version. The slash is the RFC 3261
    product-token form (matches FRITZ!OS / MicroSIP / PJSUA), so
    the version is now preserved in the server-side display.

