gsipper (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix './build.sh --pjsua2' leaving a stale 2.14.1 egg on the
    Python import path. PJSIP's setup.py installs into a versioned
    'pjsua2-<ver>-py<x.y>.egg' directory and APPENDS the path to
    easy-install.pth, so re-running the build (e.g. 2.14.1 -> 2.15)
    kept the older egg ahead of the new one — 'import pjsua2'
    silently resolved to the stale build and our --deb step then
    bundled it. The user's report:

      Adding pjsua2 2.15 to easy-install.pth file
      ...
      $ ./build.sh --deb
      >>> bundling pjsua2 from:
          /home/.../site-packages/pjsua2-2.14.1-py3.13-...egg

    Two changes:

    1) Force-rebuild's user-site cleanup now wipes ALL pjsua2*
       artefacts under ~/.local/lib/python3*/site-packages —
       pjsua2.py, _pjsua2*.so, pjsua2-*.egg/ directories,
       pjsua2*.egg-info/ — and strips any 'pjsua2' lines from
       easy-install.pth.

    2) build_pjsip no longer runs 'setup.py install --user'.
       Instead it directly copies build/lib.linux-*/_pjsua2*.so
       and pjsua2.py into the Python user-site (resolved via
       'site.getusersitepackages()'). No more egg machinery,
       no more easy-install.pth surprises.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  Final-release polish pass. Audit-driven cleanups + the focused
  CPU / UI-responsiveness items the audit surfaced.

  Real bug
  --------
    * SipEndpoint._dispose_via_worker had ~6 lines of unreachable
      code after the 'return False  # one-shot' — leftover from
      the call-state-handler merge. Deleted.

  Lower idle / in-call CPU
  ------------------------
    * pjsua2 endpoint log level lowered from 4 (DEBUG) to 3
      (INFO) — PJSIP no longer emits hundreds of per-packet
      lines per second across SWIG into our log bridge.
    * _PjLogBridge.write now short-circuits on level >= 5 BEFORE
      str()ing the entry, so the few TRACE messages that do
      sneak through don't cost an allocation + idle_add hop.
    * PlaybackDialog tick interval 250 ms -> 500 ms. 2 Hz is
      plenty for the elapsed-time label + slider, halves the
      CPU during MP3 playback.

  Snappier UI
  -----------
    * _ChatPage gains append_message(); the two callers
      (_on_chat_send and on_incoming_message) use it instead of
      refresh_messages() so a single new bubble doesn't rebuild
      every prior bubble in the conversation. refresh_messages
      stays for the open-page and status-flip paths.
    * MainWindow._lookup_contact_display caches results on
      self._contact_lookup_cache. Bursts of incoming SIP MESSAGEs
      from the same peer no longer reload contacts.json + scan
      every contact's phone digits per message.
    * ContactsView._on_contact_saved schedules the row-rebuild
      and the JSON write via GLib.idle_add so the
      AddContactDialog finishes its close animation before any
      list churn — matches the delete path landed in 1.1.1.

  Mechanical cleanup
  ------------------
    * Lifted 'import os' (calls_view) and 'import logging' (app)
      from inside functions up to module-top imports.
    * Refreshed the default_codecs() docstring; the old wording
      referenced retired G.729 / libbcg729 lore that 1.2.6 made
      obsolete.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

