gsipper (1.0.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix pjlib assertion ('Calling pjlib from unknown/external thread')
    crashing the app right after a recorded call ended. The
    AudioMediaRecorder ref was being dropped on the GTK main thread,
    so the SWIG-generated destructor invoked pjmedia cleanup off the
    pjsua2 worker. Both the call and recorder refs are now packaged
    into a no-op closure submitted to the worker after the 5-second
    grace period, so SWIG destructors run on a pjsua2-registered
    thread.
  * Fix AttributeError 'AudioMediaRecorder object has no attribute
    "delete"' — that method only exists on pj.Account. The recorder
    closes through Python refcount-driven destruction; the dedicated
    stop_recording() + take_recorder() now reflect that.

